ng), even inside a disease-defining list. Keep these O. List position alone does not make an item a disease.\n    - The state nominal is a fixed premodifier-plus-head compound (e.g., [gene] + deficiency). Label that as SpecificDisease under the lexicalized disease-name convention. It does not need the disease-defining frame, and this principle does not change it.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2526, "output_tokens": 3093, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2639}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}